resolver={
 'interface':'MaterialResolutionPort.resolve(project_uuid, owner_generation, document_uuid, captured_revision, format, ordered ReferenceRequest[]) → ResolutionSnapshot or ResolutionError. No paths or network callback in WORK/codec.',
 'request':'ReferenceRequest {source_path, kind:asset|binding, opaque_id, pinned_digest?:lowerhex64, target_id?:string}. IDs nonempty UTF8 ≤256bytes, no NUL; case-sensitive. Never interpret labels, free text or path as an asset ID without explicit registry mapping.',
 'recognition':'EssXmlV1 only /eluslotScene/architecture/eluslotArch/nodes/node/assetRefs/assetRef text is recognized legacy asset reference. Preserve exact original text; resolver registry must explicitly map it. No trim/coercion. Unknown element/attribute whose semantics are not in an adopted projector sets unsupported_projection_paths; no trusted mutation/save/clear until complete projector available. DesignJsonV1 binding/reference extraction belongs to adopted C1+H2 projector; no recursive guessing of props strings.',
 'response':'ResolutionSnapshot {project_uuid, owner_generation, document_uuid, captured_revision, catalog_revision:string, completeness:Complete, assets:[{source_path,asset_id,digest}], bindings:[{source_path,id,target_id?,state:Valid|Pending|Invalid}], root_proof_id:string}. Echo fields must match. All requested references answered exactly once; no extra/duplicate path. Catalog revision/root proof nonempty ≤256bytes. Digest lowerhex64. Sort S1 asset refs by (asset_id UTF8,digest); dedup identical pairs; conflicting digests for one ID rejected. Bindings sorted by ID; duplicate ID rejected.',
 'binding_policy':'Valid requires target in candidate entity-ID set or explicit external catalog proof. Missing internal target becomes Pending only if original authored binding explicitly declares pending; otherwise InvalidDependency. Invalid is preserved for inspection only and blocks trusted install/save/clear; no conversion to valid by dropping binding. Pending bindings retained, block execute/build capabilities; edit/save permitted only with Complete resolution and all asset versions pinned.',
 'freshness':'Owner rechecks catalog revision/root proof through resolver validate(snapshot) immediately before install/save reservation. Changed proof returns StaleDependency; retries are explicit new requests, never silent remapping. Hold pin token through in-flight transaction; release on completion/detach only after retention roots include proof/history.',
 'availability':'M05-S1 is retention policy, not catalog or physical pin implementation. Proposed production integration uses fail-closed Unavailable resolver until separately approved provider/pinning implementation accepted. Reference-free documents use locally verified Complete empty snapshot only if projector proved no reference-bearing/unknown content; never [] for unexamined material.',
 'out_of_scope':'No asset copy/delete/GC, external download, automatic version upgrade, repair, actual merge or M05 catalog implementation. New resolver signature is a proposed application output port, not an already existing Port.'}

clear={
 'prepare':'Current owner +Healthy+S1 editable+expected revision. Decode captured whole document; require Complete projection and resolution. Return server-held ClearPlan {opaque plan_id,owner_generation,session_uuid,revision,before_semantic,format,policy_version,counts,paths,expires_at}. TTL60seconds monotonic; proposed cap32plans/session, reject capacity without eviction.',
 'ess_policy':'Policy ESS-CLEAR-v1 accepts closed scaffold: root meta/work/architecture/design; meta preserved except exact volatile exclusions; work contains board, board contains task only; architecture contains eluslotArch with meta/nodes/edges; nodes only node, edges only edge; design contains meta/nodes/selection/product_pass, nodes only node. Unknown business child/attribute anywhere in cleared containers or unsupported nested node shape blocks clear with UnsupportedProjection; no silent dropping. Exact allowed attributes are the frozen sample map; sample is a deliberately restricted clear profile, not claim of complete ESS schema.',
 'ess_result':'Remove every work/board/task, every architecture node/edge, every design node, empty design selection text. Preserve empty required containers and all metadata/root format identity; product_pass must false. This clears design Form too for ESS aggregate; no insertion of synthetic defaults. Cleared nodes carry their bindings/assets out of live projection; Undo retains complete before-content and pinned versions. No filesystem deletion.',
 'design_policy':'DESIGN-CLEAR-v1: C1/H2 adopted validator must identify exactly one root Form. Keep its id/type/parent, geometry and all supported props; remove all other nodes, relations/bindings owned by removed nodes, set selection to root Form ID if field present (otherwise remain absent), keep meta optional fields exactly including 0/false/empty guides. Form-owned bindings remain and must resolve. Ambiguous root/multiple Forms/unknown relationship ownership rejects clear. No arbitrary unknown props deletion.',
 'confirm':'Request {plan_id,expected_revision,request_id}; recheck caller binding/generation/TTL/revision/before semantic/health/material proof. One S1 MutationKind::Clear prepare+commit; no-op produces unchanged revision and no Undo. Same request replay returns original receipt; changed request payload with same ID conflicts.',
 'failure':'Any error before S1 commit preserves content/revision/history/formal and snapshot baselines. Clear does not save; dirty reflects semantic delta. Undo uses existing S1 once and restores assets/bindings/metadata. No domain recovery setter.',
 'lifecycle':'Close/switch/discard cancels plans, revokes writer and Viewer capabilities. Completed save proofs remain target-scoped evidence even if session detached. Late clear confirmation never installs into replacement generation.'}

save_health={
 'capture':'Immutable S1 capture plus project/document/session/generation/request/target identity/previous raw digest/exact encoded bytes/semantic profile+digest. Freeze these before IO; no UI-provided digest or payload at save.',
 'lease':'Opaque server-selected target proof; canonical path from trusted native selection under authorized project, plus stable file/parent identity and aliases tested by target adapter. String path equality is insufficient. Existing file lease held from open through detach; SaveAs uses distinct lease and expected absent target (previous=None); existing target SaveAs rejected until separate overwrite contract.',
 'reserve':'One in-flight per owner and alias-safe target. Healthy→WriteInFlight atomic before IO, release owner lock during codec/IO; edits/clear/undo/merge/replacement/snapshot blocked; queries allowed. Proposed request cache128/session1024/runtime, no silent eviction; capacity error before IO. Completion may only resolve matching reservation.',
 'receipt':'Check canonical target, previous_digest exact Option, committed_digest SHA256 encoded bytes and nonempty transaction_id. Valid proof ACKs captured revision+semantic only, never raw hash. If live revision is newer, ACK old capture without rolling back/forcing clean. formal ACK never changes snapshot baseline.',
 'outcomes':'Saved {request_id,captured_revision,live_revision,dirty,proof_id}; CommittedAckDeferred {proof_id,reason:Detached|OwnerChanged|AckRejected}; FailedBeforeCommit {error}; RecoveryBlocked {proof_id,error}. committed/deferred cannot be reported ordinary unchanged failure or automatically retried.',
 'health':'IO RecoveryRequired or receipt mismatch→RecoveryBlocked retaining error/proof and target identity through detach. Other IO errors preserve exact details; release only matching reservation. No automatic clear on acquire success, timeout or new window. Runtime-only registry cannot claim durable uncertain-proof tracking.',
 'reopen':'RO-A explicit fresh open acquires existing FileCommitPort lease; adapter already inspects journal and rejects unresolved/invalid/mismatched journal. Acquire may create lock sidecar. Read/decode/resolve/native owner validate before install new S1 session baseline; no old ACK replay. In-runtime uncertain target remains denied across reopen. Across restart rely only on adapter journal gates; receipt-mismatch not durably attested, so complete recovery certification excluded.',
 'clear_health_policy':'No public unblock command in this slice. Diagnostic export and detach allowed; repair/attested unblock requires separately approved IO-owned recovery Port/transaction. Do not implement clear-health by rebuilding session. An explicit repair may be future work; user-facing blocked status includes target evidence.',
 'leave':'Server plan TTL60s captures owner/generation/revision. Save choice proceeds only Saved with current captured revision and no newer dirty revision; deferred/blocked/stale remains open. Discard detaches current generation after exact confirmation; Cancel changes nothing. Successful project switch revokes all matching capabilities; failure preserves current owner.',
 'dependencies':'Alias-safe native selection/identity is not established by IO raw path API. Reuse only separately adopted+accepted M01-S3 target seam; absent provider returns DependencyNotReady before acquire. This package approves integration contract, not implementation of M01-S3 or IO recovery.'}

